            <td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">829,166&#160;</span>
            </td>
            <td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Charges based on annual Transmission Revenue Requirement as approved by the FERC.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Charges based on various point to point connections.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On March 1, 2020, GridLiance Heartland LLC (GLH) became a transmission owner (TO) in the Ameren Illinois (AMIL) pricing zone of MISO, thereby joining the existing transmission owners Ameren Illinois Company (AIC), Ameren Transmission Company of Illinois (ATXI), Prairie Power, Inc., and Hoosier Energy. Each of these transmission owners is allocated a portion of the revenue collected for the AMIL pricing zone based on its respective revenue requirement. GLH, like ATXI, is not a load serving entity. The load for the AMIL pricing zone of MISO is equal to the load reported by AIC, which includes all retail and wholesale load in the pricing zone. To avoid duplication, GLH does not present the data here but, through this footnote, refers instead to the reported load data in AIC's Form No. 3Q filing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
